# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values. `.env` is gitignored.
# For Vercel, add the same variables under Project → Settings → Environment
# Variables (they must keep the VITE_ prefix to reach the browser).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Firebase ── console.firebase.google.com
# Create a project → Add app → Web. Copy the config values it shows you.
# Then: Build → Authentication → Sign-in method → enable Email/Password,
# and add ONE user (yours) under the Users tab. There is no sign-up flow.
# Then: Build → Firestore Database → Create database → production mode,
# and paste the rules from firestore.rules.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-project.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# ── Anthropic ── console.anthropic.com → API Keys
# Powers ticket extraction, chart reading, trade review, pattern analysis
# and Ask-your-journal. Everything else works without it.
#
# NOTE: this key ships to the browser. That is acceptable for a single-user
# tool you run yourself, but it means anyone who can open the deployed page
# can read the key from devtools. Keep the deployment private, set a spend
# limit on the key, and rotate it if the URL ever gets shared.
VITE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ── Cloudinary ── cloudinary.com/console
# Stores chart and ticket screenshots. Free tier is plenty.
# 1. Copy your Cloud Name from the dashboard.
# 2. Settings → Upload → Add upload preset → Signing Mode: Unsigned → Save.
# 3. Put the preset's name below.
# Without these, trades still save — the screenshots just aren't kept.
VITE_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
VITE_CLOUDINARY_UPLOAD_PRESET=
